<https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Biogeographical_Region> rdf:type owl:Class ; 
  rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Geographical_Region> ; 
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions> ; 
  rdfs:label "Biogeographical Region"@en ; 
  skos:definition "A geographical region delineated using ecological, biological, climatic, or physical characteristics."@en . 
<https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Biome_Type> rdf:type owl:Class ; 
  rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject> ; 
  rdfs:comment "Some of the instances of this class such as Mediterranean_Forests_Woodlands_And_Scrub have a specific page on the OneEarth.org site.  Those instances have an rdfs:seeAlso link to their specific page. Most of the instances do not have their own page so their rdfs:seeAlso points to the definition of a Biome Type on OneEarth."@en ; 
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions> ; 
  rdfs:label "Biome Type"@en ; 
  skos:definition "A category used to classify geographical regions by broad ecological characteristics; a biome type is a classification concept rather than a particular geographical area."@en ; 
  skos:scopeNote "The fourteen biome types are named individuals of this class. Classification by biome type is distinct from geographical parthood."@en . 
<https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Bioregion> rdf:type owl:Class ; 
  rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Biogeographical_Region> ; 
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions> ; 
  rdfs:label "Bioregion"@en ; 
  skos:definition "A geographical area delineated by One Earth using ecological patterns, physical geography, and ecoregional groupings; coastal areas may include adjoining marine areas."@en . 
<https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Country> rdf:type owl:Class ; 
  rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Political_Region> ; 
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions> ; 
  rdfs:label "Country"@en ; 
  skos:definition "A geographical region recognized as a country in the source geographical scheme."@en . 
<https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Ecoregion> rdf:type owl:Class ; 
  rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Biogeographical_Region> ; 
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions> ; 
  rdfs:label "Ecoregion"@en ; 
  skos:definition "A geographical area representing a terrestrial ecological unit used in the One Earth Bioregions Framework."@en . 
<https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Geographical_Region> rdf:type owl:Class ; 
  rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Location> ; 
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions> ; 
  rdfs:label "Geographical Region"@en ; 
  skos:definition "A spatial area treated as an identifiable place, whether delineated by biogeography, governance, or another geographical convention."@en ; 
  skos:scopeNote "This class provides a common superclass for biogeographical and political regions. Political boundaries need not coincide with ecological boundaries. Country and State are included as extension points; no political-region individuals are supplied in this release."@en . 
<https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Political_Region> rdf:type owl:Class ; 
  rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Geographical_Region> ; 
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions> ; 
  rdfs:label "Political Region"@en ; 
  skos:definition "A geographical region identified through political or administrative boundaries."@en . 
<https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Realm> rdf:type owl:Class ; 
  rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Biogeographical_Region> ; 
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions> ; 
  rdfs:label "Realm"@en ; 
  skos:definition "A geographical area used as one of the fourteen highest-level realm divisions of the One Earth Bioregions Framework."@en . 
<https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/State> rdf:type owl:Class ; 
  rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Political_Region> ; 
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions> ; 
  rdfs:label "State"@en ; 
  skos:definition "A geographical region recognized as a state-level administrative division in the source geographical scheme."@en . 
<https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Subrealm> rdf:type owl:Class ; 
  rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions/Biogeographical_Region> ; 
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions> ; 
  rdfs:label "Subrealm"@en ; 
  skos:definition "A geographical area that groups bioregions within a One Earth realm division."@en ; 
  skos:scopeNote "The source snapshot has 53 subrealms: 52 habitable subrealms and Antarctic Continent & Islands. Oceanic Islands is included as the subrealm of Oceania. No fixed cardinality is imposed."@en . 
